('74476b25-8fb4-522e-ae8b-56bcafd59fac'::uuid,'9f3a52ba-ab8e-531a-ad9a-84833f0a6ea5'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-C \\| Form 3-02 – Dataset Metadata and Quality Checklist\n\n| **Metadata / quality field**                   | **Check / entry**                                     |\n|------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------|\n| Dataset ID, title and description              | Record unique ID, purpose and content                 |\n| Source agency and original product reference   | Record issuing authority and original file            |\n| Data date, acquisition date and update cycle   | Distinguish source date from download date            |\n| Geographic coverage and scale/resolution       | Record City/barangay coverage and suitability         |\n| Coordinate reference system and units          | Record original CRS and any transformation            |\n| Method, scenario, baseline and time horizon    | Record model/method assumptions and projection period |\n| Attributes, legend and classification          | Check classes, units, code lists and interpretation   |\n| Completeness, geometry and no-data areas       | Record defects and treatment                          |\n| Limitations and uncertainty                    | Record known constraints and prohibited uses          |\n| Custodian, access classification and retention | Record responsible office and access controls         |\n| Technical validation and approval              | Reviewer, date, comments and approved use             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-C.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('33da72b2-f75d-557c-9000-6270604cd483'::uuid,'e7b3e024-7d39-52cf-a4ee-55550a7c16b8'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-D \\| Form 3-03 – CDRA Hazard-Impact Scoping Matrix\n\n| **Hazard / climate stressor** | **Source / scenario / horizon** | **Affected sectors / elements**                          | **Impact chain and spatial area**           | **Data gap / uncertainty**    | **Validation owner** |\n|-------------------------------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|----------------------|\n| \\[Enter hazard\\]              | \\[Source, date, scenario\\]      | \\[People, buildings, livelihoods, services, ecosystems\\] | \\[Initiating event → impact → consequence\\] | \\[Missing data / confidence\\] | \\[Office / agency\\]  |\n| \\[Enter hazard\\]              | \\[Source, date, scenario\\]      | \\[People, buildings, livelihoods, services, ecosystems\\] | \\[Initiating event → impact → consequence\\] | \\[Missing data / confidence\\] | \\[Office / agency\\]  |\n\nInstructions: Complete one row per hazard-sector pathway. Identify assumptions and data gaps explicitly. Do not assign risk classes outside the current DHSUD-prescribed method.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-D.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('7844d7dd-94d9-5b3e-a958-890d3801fdf9'::uuid,'90c1dec6-06ac-5832-a1f9-8b356a61d78e'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-E \\| Form 3-04 – CDRA Major Decision Area Register\n\n| **MDA ID / location**            | **Evidence and risk finding**     | **Affected people/assets / system** | **Policy or investment decision required**                                              | **Lead office / partners** | **Indicator / target / review date** |\n|----------------------------------|-----------------------------------|-------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------------------|\n| \\[ID / barangay / spatial unit\\] | \\[CDRA result and map reference\\] | \\[Disaggregated groups and assets\\] | \\[Land-use, infrastructure, social protection, ecosystem or preparedness intervention\\] | \\[Owner\\]                  | \\[Measure and due date\\]             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-E.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('097fb08d-b32f-54a9-83c8-903d303d00c0'::uuid,'46a8c9fd-c613-58c1-9879-078061eecd35'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-F \\| Form 3-05 – Critical Facilities and Dependency Register\n\n| **Asset ID / name** | **Owner / operator** | **Service / capacity / users**       | **Hazard exposure / vulnerability** | **Dependencies / downstream services**            | **Backup / redundancy / restoration**        | **Validation date**  |\n|---------------------|----------------------|--------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|----------------------|\n| \\[ID\\]              | \\[Office / utility\\] | \\[Function, capacity, service area\\] | \\[Map/source and condition\\]        | \\[Power, water, telecom, road, fuel, staff, ICT\\] | \\[Alternate, backup, estimated restoration\\] | \\[Date / signatory\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-F.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('6dde3b7c-8e48-574b-9d2d-d99675258a9c'::uuid,'9408a317-5f2d-5396-bfd1-9eaad44254d6'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-G \\| Form 3-06 – Contingency Plan Quality and Exercise Record\n\n| **Control area**                     | **Required evidence / reviewer finding**                                         | **Status / corrective action** |\n|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| Scenario and assumptions             | Source, magnitude, location, lead time, cascading effects and uncertainty        |                                |\n| Objectives and concept of operations | Priorities, phases, EOC/ICS interface and transition                             |                                |\n| Roles and tasking                    | Lead/support agencies, barangay roles, escalation and alternates                 |                                |\n| Triggers and warning                 | Authoritative source, action threshold, decision authority and dissemination     |                                |\n| Operations and protection            | Evacuation, shelter, health, logistics, protection, MHPSS and public information |                                |\n| Resources and logistics              | Personnel, equipment, supplies, transport, facilities and gaps                   |                                |\n| Information management               | Situation reporting, validation, decision log and records                        |                                |\n| Exercise results                     | Objectives, observations, decisions, performance and lessons                     |                                |\n| Corrective actions                   | Action, owner, deadline, resource and closure evidence                           |                                |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-G.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('31c573d9-1aff-5607-9742-a6cee4322fda'::uuid,'84f5dd93-d2d8-5de7-b21a-e2ff7911517c'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-H \\| Form 3-07 – Essential Functions Inventory and BIA\n\n| **Department / service** | **Essential function / legal basis** | **Service users / minimum level**          | **People / skills / succession** | **Facilities / ICT / records** | **Dependencies / suppliers**                 | **Impact over time / priority**                        | **Recovery strategy / owner**  |\n|--------------------------|--------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------|----------------------------------|--------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| \\[Office\\]               | \\[Function and authority\\]           | \\[Who depends on service; minimum output\\] | \\[Key posts, alternates\\]        | \\[Site, system, records\\]      | \\[Power, water, telecom, transport, vendor\\] | \\[Life safety, legal, welfare, financial; time bands\\] | \\[Strategy, owner, resources\\] |\n\nInstructions: Department head validates each function. Proposed recovery time and minimum service levels must be justified by BIA evidence and approved by the designated continuity executive; do not use unsupported generic time targets.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-H.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('3a207140-3a65-57b6-9883-db155bbed9a1'::uuid,'ae91e295-4eee-5511-965a-8a53ea3b2b19'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-I \\| Form 3-08 – Barangay DRRM Plan Review Status\n\n| **Barangay official name / ID** | **Master-list source** | **Plan period / version** | **Approval evidence** | **Quality tool / review date** | **Status** | **Required corrections / due date** | **Exercise / update evidence** |\n|---------------------------------|------------------------|---------------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------------|------------|-------------------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| \\[Barangay\\]                    | \\[Official source\\]    | \\[Period/version\\]        | \\[Resolution/date\\]   | \\[Tool/version/date\\]          | \\[Status\\] | \\[Action and due date\\]             | \\[Record\\]                     |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-I.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('01b041b7-4f53-5b38-9d52-90a2cdd9cf68'::uuid,'62fd7931-d11e-5a0f-b471-804bba6800ea'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-J \\| Form 3-09 – DRR/CCA Project Screening\n\n| **Project / proponent / site** | **Hazard and climate exposure** | **People/assets affected / inclusion** | **Siting/design/ecosystem implications**    | **Risk treatment / residual risk** | **Technical reviewers**               | **Planning/budget decision**           |\n|--------------------------------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------|------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|----------------------------------------|\n| \\[Project\\]                    | \\[Map/source/date/scenario\\]    | \\[Groups and service impacts\\]         | \\[Alternatives, codes, ecosystem/heritage\\] | \\[Measures, cost, residual risk\\]  | \\[CPDO/Engineering/OBO/CENRO/CDRRMO\\] | \\[LDC/LFC/Budget/approving authority\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-J.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('bc8819bc-c6ab-5a33-9e7f-99dbf9dd581c'::uuid,'26c123c7-cb03-5d9a-8dce-52900f5e108d'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-K \\| Form 3-10 – Consultation and Inclusion Validation record\n\n| **Consulted group / organization** | **Date / accessible method**       | **Risk or access issue raised** | **Evidence / location** | **Plan or design response**          | **Responsible office / closure** |\n|------------------------------------|------------------------------------|---------------------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------|\n| \\[Group\\]                          | \\[Date, language, access support\\] | \\[Issue\\]                       | \\[Evidence\\]            | \\[Response / reason if not adopted\\] | \\[Owner / due date\\]             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-K.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('4863a38e-1755-5ced-a4e8-3832f8b05646'::uuid,'d323303a-0f9e-5c64-93d6-de5b941aebca'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-L \\| Form 3-11 – Corrective Action and Document Revision Register\n\n| **Finding / source**               | **Root cause** | **Corrective action** | **Accountable owner** | **Due date / resources** | **Verification evidence** | **Closure / escalation**     |\n|------------------------------------|----------------|-----------------------|-----------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------|------------------------------|\n| \\[IAT / exercise / event / audit\\] | \\[Cause\\]      | \\[Action\\]            | \\[Office / official\\] | \\[Date / budget\\]        | \\[Record / test\\]         | \\[Closed by / escalated to\\] |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-L.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('76bec8b6-6dd0-542c-842a-ef4db186d764'::uuid,'1e6d98b2-b29d-52c9-9f6d-537cf7b2e265'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-M \\| Source and Methodology Register\n\n| **Source**                                                                        | **Verified use in this chapter**                                                                                          | **Status / qualification**                                                                                                                                                                                    |\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Republic Act No. 10121 (2010), Lawphil / Supreme Court E-Library                  | Statutory LDRRMC and LDRRMO functions; risk assessment, risk information, local risk map, LDRRMP and contingency planning | Official statutory text; apply with current IRR                                                                                                                                                               |\n| DHSUD Memorandum Circular No. 2025-004, Enhanced CDRA Policy                      | Policy intent and minimum approach for standardized enhanced CDRA                                                         | DHSUD learning repository confirms policy purpose; obtain signed circular and annexes for exact operative requirements                                                                                        |\n| DHSUD CDRA learning repository: 5-Step+ CDRA Process                              | Detailed sequence for CDRA steps and subsequent compilation, CLUP mainstreaming, M&E and communication                    | Official DHSUD training material; apply current technical parameters and prescribed tools                                                                                                                     |\n| PHIVOLCS GIS hazard-map download instructions and Hazard Assessment Services      | Source acquisition, product scale/availability caveats and limits of hazard assessment reports                            | Official PHIVOLCS pages; not a substitute for current technical manuals                                                                                                                                       |\n| DILG MC No. 2025-035 / Listo si KAP information                                   | Barangay preparedness and planning responsibilities                                                                       | DILG regional publication confirms initiative; use signed circular and current national quality tools                                                                                                         |\n| DILG Quality Assessment System / BDRRM plan template                              | Barangay plan review structure and quality assurance                                                                      | Use current official versions; legacy templates are not presumed current                                                                                                                                      |\n| OCD/NDRRMC PSCP Guidebook                                                         | Essential functions, BIA and continuity planning                                                                          | Listed in IAT References as project reference; exact edition and original file must be verified before final technical sign-off                                                                               |\n| NDRRMC–OCD Contingency Planning Guidebook (February 2020)                         | Hazard scenario and response planning method                                                                              | Supplied 8 November 2026 and applied to SOP 3-6 (CP Forms 1–11; activation and deactivation flow; the Incident Commander recommends termination). Confirm with OCD Region VIII that it is the current edition |\n| UNDRR Disaster Resilience Scorecard for Cities – Detailed Level Assessment (2017) | Good-practice benchmarks for scenarios, critical asset failure chains, risk-sensitive planning and ecosystem services     | Benchmark only; IAT crosswalk identifies its adapted indicators                                                                                                                                               |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-M.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('ae57fb41-b283-50b0-80cc-2f447151ebd7'::uuid,'3189595e-e334-59f9-829b-ac4fb4757c40'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020)',E'# ANNEX 3-N \\| Glossary of Terms Used in This Chapter\n\nTerms follow RA 10121, the DHSUD CDRA guidance and the definitions used in Chapters 1 and 2. Where an official definition exists, it governs.\n\n**Table 3.12**\n\n*Glossary of Terms*\n\n| **Term**                                    | **Meaning in this Manual**                                                                                                                                  |\n|---------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Adaptive capacity                           | The ability of people, institutions and systems to adjust to, prepare for and recover from hazard and climate impacts.                                      |\n| BIA (business impact analysis)              | Assessment of how the disruption of an essential function affects people and the City over time; the basis for recovery priorities (Form 3-07).             |\n| CDRA (Climate and Disaster Risk Assessment) | The DHSUD-prescribed assessment that links hazard and climate information to exposure, vulnerability and risk, and to land-use decisions.                   |\n| Contingency plan                            | An approved, hazard-specific plan setting scenario, triggers, roles, resources and reporting before an event (SOP 3-6).                                     |\n| Critical point facility / lifeline          | A facility (hospital, school, EOC) or network (road, power, water, telecommunications) whose failure affects many people or services.                       |\n| Exposure                                    | People, buildings, production areas, facilities and lifelines located where a hazard may occur.                                                             |\n| Failure chain                               | A traced sequence from a hazard through an asset failure to a service disruption and its consequences (SOP 3-4).                                            |\n| Form                                        | The record a step is closed on. In MODE every workflow and protocol step has a form; the Manual''s form where one exists, otherwise the one-tap step record. |\n| MDA (Major Decision Area)                   | A place or issue where CDRA results require a land-use, investment, social-protection or ecosystem decision (Form 3-04).                                    |\n| Modelled potential damage                   | The value of exposed assets that could be damaged under a model''s assumptions; not an observed loss or an annual expected loss.                             |\n| Process owner                               | The office accountable for an SOP producing its result; others are responsible, consulted or informed (Section 18).                                         |\n| Protocol                                    | A step-by-step operational checklist run at the point of action (for example warning dissemination); it records who closed each step and when.              |\n| PSCP (Public Service Continuity Plan)       | The City plan that keeps essential functions running during disruption (SOP 3-7).                                                                           |\n| Risk Information Register                   | The controlled list of risk datasets with source, custodian, date, scale, access class and version (SOP 3-2).                                               |\n| SOP (standard operating procedure)          | The approved, controlled text in the Manual that states what is done, by whom, under what authority and with what records.                                  |\n| Validation status                           | How far information has been checked: reported, preliminary, field-verified or official (Geo-COP layers; IAT evidence).                                     |\n| Workflow                                    | An SOP made executable in MODE: a sequence of steps across offices over days or weeks, each closed on its form.                                             |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch3v11_Annex_3-N.md (Chapter 3, v1.1 working draft (CP Guidebook 2020))','draft'),
('dfa15af6-b982-5600-a9ca-8b2250c23faf'::uuid,'3a03dcd8-4583-513d-8a37-b0df0d1da45a'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# ANNEX 4-A \\| IAT AND MASTER REQUIREMENTS TRACEABILITY REGISTER\n\nThis register copies the IAT v1.7 rows for A6, A7, A8 and B1.2–B1.5 (8 November 2026) and the functional master requirements linked to each indicator in the Data Dictionary v1.1. Cross-cutting requirements MR-01 and MR-12 to MR-15 apply to every indicator and are not repeated.\n\n**Table 4.40**\n\n*Assessment Rows and Chapter 4 Procedures*\n\n| **ID** | **Indicator (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | **Type** | **Score** | **Priority** | **Compliance** | **Evidence status** | **Functional MR**          | **SOP**                  |\n|--------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------|-----------|--------------|----------------|---------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------|\n| A6.1   | Hazard-specific EWS operational for flood (incl. Anilao/Malbasag river systems), rain-induced landslide, tsunami (Ormoc Bay) and tropical cyclone                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | M        | 3         | Medium       | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-01                     |\n| A6.2   | Warning thresholds linked to specific actions (alert levels -\\> pre-emptive evacuation, class/work suspension, State of Imminent Disaster request) in written protocols, built to take up NDRRMC impact-based triggers once issued                                                                                                                                                               | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-06, MR-16               | 4-02, 4-06               |\n| A6.3   | Last-mile dissemination channels tested to barangay/purok level (sirens, radio, SMS/ECBS, social media, barangay criers)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-02                     |\n| A6.4   | Warnings issued in local language (Cebuano/ Ormocanon) and accessible formats (sign language, visual alerts for PWD)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | GP       | 2         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-02                     |\n| A6.5   | Designated public information officer and risk communication plan (incl. rumor/misinformation management)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | GP       | 2         | Low          | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | 4-02                     |\n| A6.6   | IEC program on hazards and preparedness with annual reach targets                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | GP       | 2         | Low          | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-06                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A6.7   | Templates and channels for public notice of a State of Imminent Disaster and of the anticipatory actions required, incl. sector-specific impact-based advisories and reach to geographically isolated barangays                                                                                                                                                                                  | M        | 0         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-06, MR-16               | 4-02                     |\n| A7.1   | Annual training program for city personnel, BDRRMCs, schools and communities implemented                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.2   | Participation in quarterly Nationwide Simultaneous Earthquake Drill (NSED) and hazard-specific drills with evaluation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                            | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.3   | BDRRMC functionality across 85 barangays assessed (e.g., Listo si KAP) with support plan for low-functioning barangays                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | GP       | 2         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.4   | Permanent evacuation center(s) planned/established and existing ECs meet minimum standards (WASH, privacy, PWD access, child-friendly space)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | 4-06                     |\n| A7.5   | Prepositioned relief stocks/food packs and non-food items with inventory and replenishment triggers                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-08               | 4-07                     |\n| A7.6   | Inclusive DRRM: GAD, PWD, senior citizen, children, IP considerations embedded in plans and services, with vulnerable-sector representatives confirming they were engaged                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-09, MR-16, MR-18 | 4-06                     |\n| A7.7   | Schools, hospitals and critical facilities included in preparedness planning and drills                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                          | GP       | 3         | Low          | Meets GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.8   | Refresher cycle (at least annual) set for trained responders, EOC staff and BDRRMC members, with attendance tracked                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | GP       | 1         | Low          | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-18               | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A7.9   | BDRRMCs can account for residents of affected puroks within 12 hours of impact (welfare check), shown in a drill or a real event                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | GP       | 1         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-04, MR-18               | 4-06                     |\n| A8.1   | Incident Command System institutionalized: EO on ICS, trained IMT roster, pre-designated Incident Commanders                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                     | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-05                     |\n| A8.2   | Organized and trained response teams: SAR (WASAR/CSSR/HAZMAT as relevant), EMS/ambulance, fire coordination with BFP                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.3   | Response equipment and vehicles inventoried, serviceable and maintained (preventive maintenance schedule)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-08               | 4-07                     |\n| A8.4   | Emergency hotline integrated with E911 and dispatch protocol (call-taking to dispatch time tracked)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | GP       | 0         | Medium       | Below GP       | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.5   | Response clusters organized at city level mirroring national cluster approach (Food & NFI, Health, WASH, CCCM, Logistics, Search Rescue & Retrieval, Law & Order, Education, Protection, ETC, MDM)                                                                                                                                                                                               | M        | 3         | Low          | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.6   | Pre-Disaster Risk Assessment (PDRA) conducted before forecast hazards, with anticipatory actions recorded                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-16               | 4-03                     |\n| A8.7   | Management of the Dead and Missing (MDM) and Rapid Damage Assessment & Needs Analysis (RDANA) teams designated and trained                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| A8.8   | Anticipatory action protocols by hazard and lead time: office-order templates for prepositioning (relief, medical supplies, animal feed, water and power for evacuation centers), deployment of heavy equipment, transport and personnel, pre-emptive evacuation incl. livestock and pets, CCCM, and safeguarding of critical infrastructure; aligned with CPs, Oplan L!sto and evacuation plans | M        | 1         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-08, MR-16        | 4-03                     |\n| A8.9   | Anticipatory social amelioration: families identified and prioritized using CBMS or the prevailing registry; data-sharing agreements compliant with RA 10173; local guidelines for anticipatory cash or vouchers issued with the CSWDO                                                                                                                                                           | M        | 1         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-16               | Chapter 3 / 6 (see note) |\n| B1.2   | Alert/activation levels defined (e.g., White-normal, Blue-alert, Red-full activation) with hazard-based triggers and a defined EOC posture when a State of Imminent Disaster is declared                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 3         | Medium       | Compliant      | Pending validation  | MR-05, MR-16               | 4-03, 4-04               |\n| B1.3   | Activation, escalation, de-escalation and deactivation procedures with designated authority                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      | M        | 2         | High         | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-04, 4-09               |\n| B1.4   | Concept of operations documents EOC functions: coordination, information management, resource management, policy support                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-04, 4-05               |\n| B1.5   | EOC linkage to Provincial (Leyte) and Regional (OCD VIII) EOCs defined                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | M        | 2         | Medium       | Non-compliant  | Pending validation  | MR-05                      | 4-05, 4-08               |\n\n*Note.* Scores are provisional until validated. Indicators without a Chapter 4 SOP are served by Chapter 3 (A7.1–A7.3, A7.5–A7.8: training, drills, BDRRMC functionality, stockpiles, inclusion, critical facilities) or Chapter 6 (A8.3, A8.4: equipment, hotline and dispatch).\n\n**Table 4.41**\n\n*Action Plan Rows (IAT v1.7), Copied Without Change*\n\n| **ID** | **Recommended action**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | **Responsible office**                    | **Target**                          | **Status**  |\n|--------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------|-------------|\n| A6.1   | Restore and insure the flood/rain gauges; set a monthly functionality check; write an EWS SOP (planned PPA).                                                                                                                                                                     | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | 2027                                | Ongoing     |\n| A6.2   | Write the warning-action matrix (PAGASA/PHIVOLCS levels -\\> pre-emptive evacuation, class/work suspension, EOC level, SID request), built to take NDRRMC impact-based triggers when issued.                                                                                      | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A6.3   | Revise the dissemination SOP with non-telecom fallbacks (VHF, sirens, criers) and test to purok level twice a year with logs.                                                                                                                                                    | CDRRMO Operations & Warning; BDRRMCs      | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A6.4   | Maintain; add PWD-inclusive EWS (planned PPA).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | CDRRMO                                    | Q3 2027                             | Ongoing     |\n| A6.5   | Designate the PIO and write the risk communication plan, including rumour management.                                                                                                                                                                                            | CDRRMO; City Information Office           | Q1 2027                             | Not started |\n| A6.6   | Set annual reach targets per barangay and report them.                                                                                                                                                                                                                           | CDRRMO Admin & Training                   | Annual                              | Ongoing     |\n| A6.7   | Prepare SID public notice templates and sector-specific advisories with channels to isolated barangays.                                                                                                                                                                          | CDRRMO; City Information Office           | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A7.1   | Maintain; merge with the TNA plan (A2.6).                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | CDRRMO Admin & Training                   | Annual                              | Ongoing     |\n| A7.2   | Maintain.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | CDRRMO                                    | Quarterly                           | Ongoing     |\n| A7.3   | Maintain; target low-functioning barangays first.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                | CDRRMO; DILG CLGOO                        | Annual                              | Ongoing     |\n| A7.4   | Audit ECs against RA 12076/DSWD standards; prioritise retrofits for the 46 critical flood barangays.                                                                                                                                                                             | CDRRMO; City Engineer; CSWDO              | 2027                                | Ongoing     |\n| A7.5   | Maintain; add AA prepositioning triggers.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | CSWDO; CDRRMO                             | Before typhoon season (May 2027)    | Ongoing     |\n| A7.6   | Hold a short FGD with PWD, senior, women and youth representatives to confirm engagement.                                                                                                                                                                                        | CDRRMO; GAD Focal Point                   | Q1 2027                             | Not started |\n| A7.7   | Maintain; include schools and hospitals in the next CP tabletop.                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | CDRRMO; DepEd; CHO                        | Q2 2027 (CP tabletop)               | Ongoing     |\n| A7.8   | Set an annual refresher cycle for responders, EOC staff and BDRRMC members and track attendance.                                                                                                                                                                                 | CDRRMO Admin & Training                   | 2027                                | Not started |\n| A7.9   | Add a 12-hour welfare-check step to BDRRMC protocols, using purok household lists (CBMS) and the CDRA exposed-household counts; test it in the next drill and log the time taken.                                                                                                | BDRRMCs; CDRRMO                           | Next drill (Q1 2027)                | Not started |\n| A8.1   | Issue a Mayor''s EO implementing CDRRMC Res. 09 s.2024: pre-designated Incident Commanders by hazard and event type, IMT roster (2 deep), delegation of authority form, and the EOC-IMT interface (B6.1); complete ICS training (A2.6) and record ICS use in the next activation. | CDRRMO; Mayor''s Office; City Legal Office | Q1 2027 (EO); training through 2027 | Ongoing     |\n| A8.2   | Update the response team EO and the BFP MOA; keep certificates current.                                                                                                                                                                                                          | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | Q1 2027                             | Not started |\n| A8.3   | Program a PM schedule for vehicles and equipment and keep logs.                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | CDRRMO; GSO                               | Q1 2027                             | Ongoing     |\n| A8.4   | Integrate the hotline with E911 and write the dispatch SOP with response-time tracking.                                                                                                                                                                                          | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | 2027                                | Not started |\n| A8.5   | Assess cluster capability and adopt a cluster EO aligned to the national response clusters (RDRRMOC SOPG 2022, Table 6: 11 clusters), naming lead and member offices.                                                                                                            | CDRRMO; cluster lead offices              | Q2 2027                             | Ongoing     |\n| A8.6   | Maintain; record anticipatory actions in each PDRA.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | CDRRMO                                    | Each forecast event                 | Ongoing     |\n| A8.7   | Designate MDM and RDANA teams by EO and train them.                                                                                                                                                                                                                              | CDRRMO; CHO; PNP                          | 2027                                | Not started |\n| A8.8   | Write AA protocols by hazard and lead time with office-order templates; walk them through in a PDRA tabletop to reach 3.                                                                                                                                                         | CDRRMO                                    | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| A8.9   | Issue local guidelines with CSWDO for anticipatory cash/vouchers using CBMS, with a DSA.                                                                                                                                                                                         | CSWDO; CDRRMO; City DPO                   | 2027                                | Not started |\n| B1.2   | Write the activation matrix using NDRRMC Memo 131 s.2018 triggers (9.2.1) and standard alert codes, with the SID posture (IRR Rule IV Sec. 1). Use the RDRRMOC SOPG 2022 alert model (White/Blue/Red; Standby/Alpha/Bravo/Charlie protocols) as the template.                    | CDRRMO Operations & Warning               | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| B1.3   | Add escalation/de-escalation/deactivation steps and authority (NDRRMC Memo 131 s.2018 deactivation triggers; RDRRMOC SOPG 2022 raising and downgrading rules) to EOC Manual Ch.2.                                                                                                | CDRRMO                                    | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| B1.4   | Write the ConOps in EOC Manual Ch.2 around the five NDRRMC Memo 131 s.2018 functions: Management, Operations, Planning, Logistics, Finance/Admin.                                                                                                                                | CDRRMO                                    | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n| B1.5   | Write the vertical coordination protocol (reporting times by alert level, channels, RDRRMC 24-h reply for SID requests).                                                                                                                                                         | CDRRMO                                    | Jan 2027 (with MOP)                 | Ongoing     |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch4v1_Annex_4-A.md (Chapter 4, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('8b022bcd-ab5f-511a-96f4-8fbf2a7d0d09'::uuid,'65b84ccd-4200-5e2b-8ada-e6d670cbc855'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# ANNEX 4-B \\| EOC AND INCIDENT COORDINATION RACI WITH LEGAL DECISION AUTHORITY\n\nOperational accountability (A) and legal decision authority are different things. The second column names who decides in law or under a City issuance; the other columns repeat the proposed RACI of section 15.\n\n**Table 4.42**\n\n*Legal Decision Authority and Operational Accountability*\n\n| **Activity**                             | **Legal or formal decision authority**                                                    | **Process-accountable (A)**           | **Responsible (R)**                                        |\n|------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Warning receipt and verification         | None (no decision)                                                                        | CDRRMO Head                           | Operations and Warning (OpCen)                             |\n| Warning-action recommendation            | Official or body named in the approved CP or EOC EO                                       | CDRRMO Head (technical process)       | Operations and Warning                                     |\n| Evacuation and public protective action  | Official or body named by law and City issuance                                           | Competent authority                   | Barangays (implementation); CDRRMO (recommendation)        |\n| Raising or lowering the EOC alert status | Official designated in the EOC EO; LGU by EO on LDRRMC recommendation (DILG VIII s. IV.3) | Designated authority                  | EOC Manager (implementation); CDRRMO Head (recommendation) |\n| EOC coordination and reporting           | Mayor/CDRRMC for policy decisions                                                         | CDRRMO Head (institutional oversight) | EOC Manager and sections                                   |\n| Field incident command                   | Incident Commander under the ICS EO                                                       | Incident Commander / IMT              | Agencies within their command                              |\n| Resource requests with expenditure       | Authorised officials under Chapter 5                                                      | CDRRMO Head                           | EOC sections; asset owners                                 |\n| SitRep submission                        | Approving official in the reporting route                                                 | CDRRMO Head (oversight)               | EOC Planning / situation unit                              |\n| Deactivation and transition              | Official designated in the EOC EO, on the IC recommendation                               | Designated authority                  | EOC Manager; sector offices                                |\n| State of Imminent Disaster               | Mayor by EO after the RA 12287 route (SOP GOV-05)                                         | CDRRMO Head as CDRRMC secretariat     | See Chapter 1                                              |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch4v1_Annex_4-B.md (Chapter 4, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('907b7f59-18d6-5b5c-855c-f8d9e9990db4'::uuid,'35d5f0ee-1c6a-52de-adec-5234a23a0022'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# ANNEX 4-C \\| HAZARD-SPECIFIC WARNING AND ACTIVATION MATRIX REGISTER\n\nThe City matrix is kept as a controlled register, one entry per hazard and scenario. Table 4.43 is the entry template. Table 4.44 summarises the regional reference triggers; they are not City thresholds until adopted.\n\n**Table 4.43**\n\n*Matrix Register Entry*\n\n| **Field**                        | **Content**                                                                               |\n|----------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Hazard and scenario**          | Hazard, scenario ID and contingency plan (with version)                                   |\n| **Authoritative source product** | Agency, product name and the exact category or wording that triggers the entry            |\n| **Adopted by**                   | EOC EO or contingency plan, with number and date; "regional reference only" until adopted |\n| **Alert status and actions**     | White, Blue or Red; actions with lead office for each                                     |\n| **Decision authority**           | Official or body who decides each action                                                  |\n| **Target groups and channels**   | Barangays, facilities and groups; primary and backup channels; accessible formats         |\n| **Acknowledgement**              | Who must confirm receipt and by when                                                      |\n| **Review**                       | Last review date, exercise and corrective actions                                         |\n\n**Table 4.44**\n\n*Regional Conditions and Triggers for Raising the Alert Status (Summary)*\n\n| **Hazard**                                                                    | **White**                                                                                                      | **Blue**                                                                                         | **Red**                                                                                                              |\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Tropical cyclone (flooding, storm surge, severe wind)                         | Weather advisories from PAGASA                                                                                 | PDRA result; Severe Weather Bulletin; tropical depression expected to enter the PAR (TCWS No. 1) | Severe Weather Bulletin; within the PAR; tropical storm (TCWS No. 2) or stronger                                     |\n| Other weather disturbances (monsoon, ITCZ, LPA, tail-end of a frontal system) | Yellow rainfall advisory: 7.5–15 mm observed in 1 hour and expected to continue for 2 hours; flooding possible | Orange rainfall advisory: 15–30 mm in 1 hour, expected to continue; flooding threatening         | Red rainfall advisory: more than 30 mm in 1 hour, expected to continue; serious flooding expected in low-lying areas |\n| El Niño and La Niña                                                           | Watch alert; climate outlook                                                                                   | Needs mobilisation of national resources                                                         | Needs extensive mobilisation of resources                                                                            |\n| Earthquake                                                                    | No damage reported; no tsunami threat                                                                          | Intensity VI expected or reported; minor sea-level disturbance                                   | Intensity VII or above; tsunami warning                                                                              |\n| Tsunami                                                                       | No tsunami threat; sea-level monitoring                                                                        | Minor sea-level disturbance: waves under 1 m above expected tides                                | Destructive tsunami: life-threatening waves over 1 m above expected tides; immediate response                        |\n\n*Note.* Summarised from Table 2, Conditions and Triggers in Raising the Alert Status, of the DILG VIII Disaster Response Reporting Template and SOP (RDRRMC VIII Resolution No. 12-006, s. 2023). Either one listed condition or the result of the PDRA or NDRRMC meetings applies. The table also covers volcanoes, tornadoes, conflict, fire, maritime and aviation incidents, CBRNE, epidemics and special events; consult the source for those. Rainfall categories are PAGASA products; the City does not set its own rainfall numbers.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch4v1_Annex_4-C.md (Chapter 4, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('926a5a4c-28bd-5bf4-b650-a3e21a3147c3'::uuid,'4a1db36a-0364-55dc-a164-3a87bbc73f09'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# ANNEX 4-D \\| GAWAD KALASAG CY 2026 EVIDENCE CROSSWALK\n\nThe Gawad KALASAG LDRRMO assessment toolkit (CY 2026) asks for evidence that Chapter 4 records already produce. Keeping the records as the procedures require produces that evidence as a by-product.\n\n**Table 4.45**\n\n*Chapter 4 Records Used as Gawad KALASAG Means of Verification*\n\n| **Toolkit criterion (CY 2026)**                | **Means of verification asked for**                                                                                                         | **Chapter 4 record or procedure**                                      | **Where it is kept**                                           |\n|------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Established local DRRM operations center (1.8) | EO or similar issuance creating a 24/7 OpCen; OpCen duty logbook; identified alternate EOC                                                  | SOP HR-05 handover (HR-F04); SOP 4-01 log; alternate EOC under SOP 3-7 | MODE: logbook, DRRM protocols; Vault: the EO                   |\n| Early warning system (A.2, 2.3)                | SOP or manual on EWS covering risk knowledge, monitoring and warning, dissemination and communication, response capability                  | SOP 4-01, 4-02; matrix register (Annex 4-C); EWR-F01, EWR-F03          | Library: Chapter 4; MODE: protocol runs                        |\n| Response under alert conditions                | Order or memorandum raising and downgrading the alert status; PDRA attendance and minutes; deployment memorandum; ICS forms; timely reports | SOP 4-03, 4-04, 4-05, 4-08, 4-09; EOC-F01, EWR-F04, EOC-F03, EOC-F05   | MODE: EOC level history, SitReps, protocol runs; Vault: orders |\n| Contingency plans                              | LDRRMC-approved, Sanggunian-adopted hazard-specific plans for at least the top two hazards                                                  | Chapter 3 SOP 3-6; activation in SOP 4-04                              | MODE: EOC → Plans and clusters; Vault                          |\n| ICS in place                                   | Updated IMT organisational structure; IMT members trained; AAR of a SIMEX based on the SOP or CP                                            | SOP 4-05; SOP 4-09 AAR (ER-F06)                                        | MODE: roster, protocol runs; Vault: AARs                       |\n\n*Note.* Criteria and means of verification paraphrased from the OCD Gawad KALASAG LDRRMO assessment toolkit, CY 2026 (checklists S, C and MS). The toolkit governs; this crosswalk only shows where the evidence is kept.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch4v1_Annex_4-D.md (Chapter 4, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('d8018c84-8624-5fde-8050-f8200fbbde90'::uuid,'5dd059f9-29d7-5059-a659-a11a61bed766'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0',E'# Annex 6-A. IAT and Master Requirements Traceability\n\n**Table 6.41**\n\n*IAT Rows, Master Requirements and Chapter 6 Procedures*\n\n| **IAT** | **Type**     | **w** | **Score** | **Gap priority** | **Master requirements**              | **SOP**          | **Recommended action (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                              |\n|---------|--------------|-------|-----------|------------------|--------------------------------------|------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| A3.5    | M            | 3     | 3         | 4.5 Medium       | MR-03; MR-04; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-01             | Tag each LDRRMFIP item to an LDRRMP and CDP PPA code; show the AA line and the EOC operations line; file the SP act adopting the CY 2026 plan. |\n| A4.1    | M            | 3     | 3         | 4.5 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-01             | Show the computation on estimated regular revenue (NTA and local sources); correct the base if only the NTA was used.                          |\n| A4.2    | M            | 3     | 3         | 4.5 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-01, 6-04       | Maintain the 70/30 split; show the AA sub-allocation inside the 70%.                                                                           |\n| A4.3    | M            | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-03             | Keep an STF ledger by year of origin with the five-year deadline; list STF balances as an AA source.                                           |\n| A4.4    | GP           | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-02             | Track utilisation quarterly in the CDRRMC; flag PPAs at risk by Q3; programme aged balances first.                                             |\n| A4.5    | M            | 2     | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-06, 6-07       | Update the pre-qualified supplier list each year; set framework agreements for relief goods, fuel and heavy equipment, usable for AA.          |\n| A4.6    | M            | 2     | 0         | 12.0 High        | MR-08; MR-16; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-01, 6-03, 6-05 | Put an AA line (up to 10% of the 70%) in the LDRRMFIP under CDP PPA 3.15; map other sources; write release steps with the tranche rule.        |\n| A4.7    | GP           | 1     | 3         | 1.0 Low          | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-09             | Check GSIS cover of the EOC, evacuation centres and City critical facilities; set priorities from the CDRA list.                               |\n| A4.8    | M            | 2     | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-10             | Set an internal audit check of the LDRRMF before year-end.                                                                                     |\n| A4.9    | GP           | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-09             | Cost response and early recovery for a Thelma-type flash flood and a Yolanda-type typhoon; record the shortfall and fallback sources.          |\n| A7.5    | M            | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-04; MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-11             | Maintain; validate the warehouse inventory and replenishment triggers; add AA prepositioning triggers.                                         |\n| A8.3    | M            | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-05; MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-12             | Programme a preventive maintenance schedule for vehicles and equipment and keep logs.                                                          |\n| A10.5   | M            | 1     | 2         | 3.0 Low          | MR-07; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-02             | Maintain; attach posting proof.                                                                                                                |\n| B6.3    | M            | 2     | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-12             | Extend the inventory to barangays, partners and suppliers.                                                                                     |\n| B6.4    | GP           | 1     | 2         | 2.0 Low          | MR-08; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 6-08             | Write the donations and volunteer SOP under SP Res. No. 2024-102.                                                                              |\n| B6.6    | GP           | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-16; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 6-06, 6-12       | Sign agreements listing item, quantity, trigger and contact, usable for AA.                                                                    |\n| B7.5    | M            | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-04; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 6-01             | Keep the EOC operations line in each LDRRMFIP.                                                                                                 |\n| A10.8   | M            | 2     | 0         | 12.0 High        | MR-07; MR-11; MR-16; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 6-05 step 8      | Prepare the 45-day post-declaration report template (Chapter 7) and confirm the route with OCD VIII.                                           |\n| C1.2    | CPDO; Budget | 1     | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 6-01 step 4      | Add a one-page DRR-CCA screening form to LDC/LFC project review, owned by the CPDO with CDRRMO sign-off.                                       |\n\n*Note.* Copied from IAT v1.7 and the Traceability and Data Dictionary v1.2. Scores and priorities are for validation (Methodology v1.1, section 6). Part C rows carry the lead office in the Type column and are not added to the IMI.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch6v1_Annex_6-A.md (Chapter 6, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0)','draft'),
('9ccebfe8-5779-5fb7-9277-396d704bd951'::uuid,'70916b63-9696-5ef7-b223-aea1ac114527'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0',E'# Annex 6-B. Pre-audit Checklist for DRRM Transactions\n\nUsed in SOP 6-10 step 1, before year-end, by CDRRMO Administration and Training with the City Accountant. Each "No" becomes a corrective action on FIN-F11. The checklist prevents the findings COA most often raises on LDRRMF use; it does not replace COA''s own requirements.\n\n**Table 6.42**\n\n*Pre-audit Checklist*\n\n| **No.** | **Check**                                                                                                           | **Evidence**                                                 | **Yes / No / NA** |\n|---------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------|\n| 1       | The LDRRMF was computed on estimated revenue from regular sources, and the computation is filed                     | FIN-F01 signed by the Budget Officer                         |                   |\n| 2       | The 70/30 split appears in the appropriation and in the books                                                       | Appropriation ordinance; ledgers                             |                   |\n| 3       | Every charge to the 70% is in the approved LDRRMFIP and is a DRRM use                                               | LDRRMFIP line; obligation request                            |                   |\n| 4       | Every QRF charge refers to an SP declaration of a State of Calamity in force at the time                            | SP resolution; FIN-F05                                       |                   |\n| 5       | Every AA charge refers to a State of Imminent Disaster in force, is within the AA line and passed the tranche check | Mayor''s EO; FIN-F06                                          |                   |\n| 6       | Unused QRF and 70% balances were transferred to the STF at year-end                                                 | Closing entries                                              |                   |\n| 7       | The STF ledger shows each balance by year of origin and its deadline; no balance passed five years unused           | FIN-F04                                                      |                   |\n| 8       | Each emergency procurement has its written ground, HoPE approval, documents and posting                             | FIN-F07; BAC records                                         |                   |\n| 9       | Each delivery has an inspection and acceptance report                                                               | IAR                                                          |                   |\n| 10      | Relief goods and non-food items issued have issue slips and distribution summaries                                  | Issue slips; summaries (no personal data in the CDRRMO file) |                   |\n| 11      | No stock on hand is past its expiry date; rotated items have issue records                                          | LOG-F01; count report                                        |                   |\n| 12      | Cash advances for DRRM operations were liquidated within the period                                                 | Liquidation reports                                          |                   |\n| 13      | Donations have acceptance documents, receipts and use records                                                       | FIN-F09; ORs                                                 |                   |\n| 14      | Quarterly utilisation reports were submitted to the CDRRMC and posted under the Full Disclosure Policy              | FIN-F03; posting proof                                       |                   |\n| 15      | DRRM property is on the asset register, covered by PAR or ICS, and counted this year                                | Count report                                                 |                   |\n| 16      | Insurance of DRRM buildings, warehouses and equipment is current                                                    | GSIS policy schedule                                         |                   |\n| 17      | Prior-year COA observations on DRRM funds, stocks and property have a reply and status                              | FIN-F11                                                      |                   |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch6v1_Annex_6-B.md (Chapter 6, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0)','draft'),
('48ef3766-c95e-5477-88a2-737aea98ef49'::uuid,'5158987f-c383-5e1b-9579-4e44f391eac2'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0',E'# Annex 6-C. Anticipatory Action Funding Pathway and Tranche Worksheet\n\nBasis: RA 12287 and its IRR (signed 14 September 2026), Rule V Secs. 1–3; ADR-025. The official text governs. DBM–COA guidelines on AA funds and NDRRMC operational guidelines are pending; this worksheet will be revised when they are issued.\n\n1.  **Plan.** The LDRRMFIP carries an AA line of no more than 10% of the 70% component, naming the AA measures (by hazard and sector), lead offices and procurement mode (SOP 6-01).\n\n2.  **Pre-arrange.** Framework agreements, supplier lists and stock plans cover AA items (SOPs 6-06, 6-11).\n\n3.  **Declare.** The City Mayor declares a State of Imminent Disaster after the PDRA, CDRRMC recommendation and RDRRMC process (Chapter 1, SOP GOV-05).\n\n4.  **Release.** Budget, Accounting and Treasury release funds immediately, within the tranche rule (SOP 6-05).\n\n5.  **Deliver.** Lead offices carry out AA measures; the No Regrets Principle applies.\n\n6.  **Lift and report.** The declaration lifts on hazard occurrence or on the Mayor''s lifting; unused AA funds accrue to the STF; the 45-day report includes AA fund use (Chapter 7).\n\n**Table 6.43**\n\n*Tranche Worksheet for Hydrometeorological and Geological Hazards*\n\n| **Line** | **Item**                                                      | **Formula**             | **Example (CY 2026 base)** |\n|----------|---------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------|----------------------------|\n| a        | LDRRMF for the year                                           | From FIN-F01            | PHP 139,955,741.40         |\n| b        | 70% component                                                 | a × 0.70                | PHP 97,969,018.98          |\n| c        | AA line in the LDRRMFIP                                       | not more than b × 0.10  | up to PHP 9,796,901.90     |\n| d        | Cap for interventions more than 3 days before forecast impact | c × 0.30                | PHP 2,939,070.57           |\n| e        | Allowance for interventions within 3 days of forecast impact  | c × 0.70                | PHP 6,857,831.33           |\n| f        | Already disbursed this year from the AA line                  | From FIN-F06            | —                          |\n| g        | Available for this declaration                                | c − f, split by d and e | —                          |\n\n*Note.* Illustration only: the CY 2026 plan has no AA line, and the base may change once the Budget Office confirms the regular-revenue computation (A4.1). Sources not subject to graduation: STF balances within their five-year period; partner, private and international donors; ODA; other LGUs; other lawful sources (IRR Rule V Secs. 1(b) and 2). Slow-onset hazards are not graduated until the NDRRMC guidelines issue, but never exceed the year''s AA line (ADR-025 item 4).\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch6v1_Annex_6-C.md (Chapter 6, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0)','draft'),
('684d6320-7f9c-5e43-8f81-c7569ae06c64'::uuid,'041b6980-a73c-572a-abd6-65df749fb4f9'::uuid,'v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0',E'# Annex 6-D. Prepositioned Stock Planning Worksheet\n\nUsed in SOP 6-11 step 1. One worksheet per priority hazard scenario; the highest result per item sets the level. Figures are entered by the CSWDO and the CDRRMO from the approved contingency plans; none is set in this Manual.\n\n**Table 6.44**\n\n*Stock Planning Worksheet*\n\n| **Line** | **Item**                                                     | **Formula or source**                            | **Entry** |\n|----------|--------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------------------------------|-----------|\n| a        | Hazard and scenario                                          | Contingency plan (Chapter 3)                     |           |\n| b        | Families to be served, by cluster of barangays               | CP Forms; CDRA exposure                          |           |\n| c        | Days of self-reliance before augmentation                    | CP; DSWD Field Office VIII                       |           |\n| d        | Packs per family per day (food) / kits per family (non-food) | CSWDO standard                                   |           |\n| e        | Target level by item                                         | b × c × d (food); b × d (kits)                   |           |\n| f        | National minimum                                             | DPMS Vol. 2: 500 food packs and 500 hygiene kits | 500 / 500 |\n| g        | Level adopted                                                | Higher of e and f                                |           |\n| h        | Procurement or call-off lead time (days)                     | FIN-F08 agreement                                |           |\n| i        | Average daily issue in an event                              | Past events; AARs                                |           |\n| j        | Reorder point                                                | h × i, plus a safety margin set by the CSWDO     |           |\n| k        | Warehouse split                                              | By cluster and hazard exposure (LOG-F02)         |           |\n| l        | Annual cost of holding and rotation                          | Into the stock replenishment line (SOP 6-01)     |           |\n\n# Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 6.45**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Item**                                                          | **Source used**                                                             | **Status**                                                                         |\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| CY 2026 LDRRMF figures                                            | CDRRMC Res. No. 05, s. 2025                                                 | Verify SP adoption of the CY 2026 plan                                             |\n| LDRRMF base                                                       | Res. No. 05, s. 2025 (NTA only)                                             | Budget Office to confirm                                                           |\n| AA rules                                                          | RA 12287 IRR Rule V, certified true copy read 11–12 Nov 2026                | Medium confidence until the City Legal Office confirms; DBM–COA guidelines pending |\n| Emergency procurement ground and documents                        | RA 12009 Sec. 35(b); GPPB Circular No. 06-2026                              | Confirm IRR details with the BAC Secretariat                                       |\n| Framework agreements                                              | RA 12009 Sec. 16; GPPB Circular No. 07-2026 (23 Jul 2026)                   | Confirm templates with the BAC Secretariat                                         |\n| "GPPB Circular 08-2026" on emergency and anticipatory procurement | Named in the Coherence Analysis (Part III.1)                                | Not found on the GPPB site on 12 Nov 2026; not cited until a copy is obtained      |\n| JMC 2013-1 provisions                                             | Secondary sources (COA 2014 DRRM audit; DBM LBC 130)                        | Check against a certified copy                                                     |\n| COA Circular No. 2012-002 section on trust-fund transfers         | Planning guide cites section 4 (4.4); a 2021 COA audit cites section 5.1.10 | Verify against the COA original before citing a section number                     |\n| DPMS Vol. 2 stock minimum                                         | NDRRMC Disaster Preparedness Minimum Standards Vol. 2, pp. 7 and 13         | Confirm the current edition with OCD VIII                                          |\n| Donations                                                         | SP Res. No. 2024-102                                                        | Confirm the acceptance delegation                                                  |\n| Platform template codes                                           | Seed of 12 Nov 2026 (WF-SOP5-xx)                                            | Re-seed as WF-SOP6-xx with aliases                                                 |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch6v1_Annex_6-D.md (Chapter 6, v1.1 working draft (IAT v1.7); renumbered from Chapter 5 Draft 1.0)','draft'),
('58404cb3-4a0c-5c65-ac4f-dfafc1b70622'::uuid,'a77a3f29-f160-5f96-ac25-e8bbb357e6e8'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 5-A. IAT and Master Requirements Traceability Register\n\n**Table 5.39**\n\n*IAT v1.7 Rows Traced to Chapter 5*\n\n| **ID** | **M/GP** | **Score** | **Priority** | **MR links** | **Recommended action (workbook)**                                                              | **Responsible office (Action Plan)**         | **Target**             | **Status**  |\n|--------|----------|-----------|--------------|--------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------|------------------------|-------------|\n| A9.1   | GP       | 1         | Medium       | MR-11        | Form and train a PDNA team using OCD templates.                                                | CDRRMO Research & Planning                   | 2027                   | Not started |\n| A9.2   | M        | 2         | Medium       | MR-11        | Maintain; state assumptions in projections.                                                    | CDRRMO                                       | After each major event | Ongoing     |\n| A9.3   | GP       | 1         | Low          | MR-11        | Add a recovery monitoring matrix to the event database (A5.4).                                 | CDRRMO Research & Planning                   | Q3 2027                | Not started |\n| A9.4   | GP       | 2         | Low          | MR-11        | Write referral pathways with CSWDO, CHO and PESO.                                              | CSWDO; CHO; PESO                             | Q3 2027                | Not started |\n| A9.5   | GP       | 1         | Medium       | MR-11; MR-18 | Use the OCD/World Bank Ready to Rebuild workbook to prepare a pre-disaster recovery framework. | CDRRMO Research & Planning                   | 2027                   | Not started |\n| A8.7   | M        | 2         | Medium       | MR-05        | Designate MDM and RDANA teams by EO and train them.                                            | CDRRMO; CHO; PNP                             | 2027                   | Not started |\n| A10.6  | GP       | 2         | Medium       | MR-07; MR-11 | Maintain.                                                                                      | CDRRMO                                       | After each event       | Ongoing     |\n| A3.4   | M        | 2         | Medium       | MR-10        | Complete the PSCP using the PSCP Guidebook.                                                    | CDRRMO Research & Planning; all city offices | Q2 2027                | Ongoing     |\n\n*Note.* Copied from the A_CDRRMO and Action_Plan sheets of IAT v1.7 and the Indicator_Data_Dictionary sheet of the Traceability workbook v1.2 without change, except that recommended actions are shortened where marked by the workbook text. Priority bands computed with the workbook formula. Evidence validation status: "Pending validation" for every row. Resources and budget source for each row are in the Action Plan sheet.\n\n**Table 5.40**\n\n*Part C Interface Rows Used by Chapter 5*\n\n| **ID** | **Indicator (summarised)**                                                    | **Lead office**                           | **Score** | **Priority** | **Chapter 5 use**                    |\n|--------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------|-----------|--------------|--------------------------------------|\n| C1.3   | CDRA estimates losses beyond physical assets                                  | CPDO                                      | 2         | Low          | Loss estimation in PDNA and baseline |\n| C1.4   | Risk-sensitive development guidelines in zoning and permits                   | CPDO; Zoning Administrator                | 2         | Medium       | Siting check in SOP 5-05             |\n| C2.1   | Structural safety of EOC, evacuation centres and critical facilities assessed | City Engineer / Building Official         | 1         | High         | Design check in SOP 5-05             |\n| C2.2   | Restoration-priority arrangements with power, water and telecoms              | CDRRMO with utility providers             | 2         | Medium       | Lifeline restoration in section 10   |\n| C2.3   | Transport anticipatory actions and alternate routes                           | City Engineer; traffic office; DPWH; port | 1         | Medium       | Road and bridge BBB criteria         |\n| C3.3   | Environmental anticipatory actions incl. safe debris disposal                 | CENRO; City Engineer; GSO                 | 1         | Medium       | Debris and waste in section 10       |\n\n*Note.* Part C rows have no Mandatory items and feed the separate Interface Index, never the Institutional Maturity Index. Priority uses the factor 1.0 for all Part C rows.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch5v1_Annex_5-A.md (Chapter 5, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('f03bf2a9-ef41-5803-b83c-445f3acaa437'::uuid,'4e4e65a0-6865-52e2-a314-05fab33c5395'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 5-B. Recovery RACI With Legal Decision Authority\n\n**Table 5.41**\n\n*Legal Decision Authority Kept Apart From Operational Accountability*\n\n| **Decision**                                            | **Legal or approving authority**                          | **Operational accountable owner (A)**          |\n|---------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------|\n| **Adoption of the pre-disaster recovery framework**     | CDRRMC                                                    | CDRRMO Head                                    |\n| **Conduct of a City PDNA**                              | CDRRMC                                                    | CDRRMO Head                                    |\n| **Approval of the PDNA**                                | CDRRMC (RDRRMC VIII review when NDRRMF funding is sought) | PDNA coordinator                               |\n| **Approval of the rehabilitation and recovery program** | Sangguniang Panlungsod, on CDRRMC endorsement             | CPDO (technical lead)                          |\n| **Appropriations and supplemental budgets**             | Sangguniang Panlungsod                                    | City Budget Officer                            |\n| **Building permits and structural acceptance**          | Building Official                                         | Proponent office                               |\n| **Land use and zoning changes**                         | Sangguniang Panlungsod (ordinance)                        | CPDO / Zoning Administrator                    |\n| **Relocation and resettlement**                         | Authorities under RA 7279 and DHSUD rules                 | Housing office with CSWDO                      |\n| **Eligibility for social services**                     | Each service office under its rules                       | CSWDO, CHO, PESO, City Agriculture as relevant |\n| **Procurement awards**                                  | Head of procuring entity on BAC recommendation            | BAC secretariat (Chapter 6)                    |\n\n*Note.* Authorities follow the NEDA (2020) guide and the general legal framework; the City Legal Office shall confirm each row before adoption.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch5v1_Annex_5-B.md (Chapter 5, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft')
